      <pubStmt/>
      <notesStmt>
        <annot>Gradual-troper of Nevers, 12th century; for SS. Marius and Martha, f. 31r. Neume division, shapes and facsimile zones: a close reading of Gallica's image of f. 31r (October 2026), written in the french hand on the manuscript's ruling (red F, yellow c and two dry-point lines) with its F clef.</annot>
      </notesStmt>
      <sourceDesc>
